1. Chosen Development Model
Agile 
Justification:
The system requires continuous updates and improvements (e.g., new features like notifications, tracking).
Requirements may evolve based on parent and daycare feedback.
Agile allows incremental delivery, meaning features like login, tracking, and notifications can be built step-by-step.
It supports flexibility and adaptability, which is essential for a user-centered system.

2. User Requirements
a. Stakeholders (WHO is involved)

| Stakeholder        | Role         | Interest                                          |
| ------------------ | ------------ | ------------------------------------------------- |
| Parents            | End-users    | Monitor child activities, ensure safety           |
| Daycare Staff      | System users | Update child information (meals, sleep, behavior) |
| Daycare Admin      | Manager      | Manage users, monitor system usage                |
| Developers         | Builders     | Develop and maintain the system                   |
| Security Personnel | Safety       | Ensure secure child pickup                        |

b. User Stories (WHAT they need and WHY)

1. As a parent, I want to receive real-time updates so that I know my child is safe.
2. As a parent, I want to see photos of my child so that I feel reassured.
3. As a parent, I want notifications when my child is picked up so that I am informed instantly.
4. As a parent, I want a safe-word system so that only authorized people can pick up my child.
5. As a staff member, I want to log meals so that parents know what their child has eaten.
6. As a staff member, I want to record sleep times so that parents can track rest patterns.
7. As a staff member, I want to log behavior notes so that parents stay informed.
8. As an admin, I want to manage users so that the system stays organized.
9. As an admin, I want to assign children to parents so that data is correctly linked.
10. As a parent, I want to access history reports so that I can review my child’s daily activities.

