5. Application Specifications (How the system is built technically)
a. Architecture
The system follows a three-tier architecture:
Frontend: User interface (parents, staff, admin)
Backend: Handles logic, authentication, notifications
Database: Stores user data, child records, activities
Flow:
Frontend → Backend → Database → Backend → Frontend
b. Database Model
-Tables
Users (id, name, email, password, role)
Children (id, name, age, parent_id)
Activities (id, child_id, type, description, timestamp)
Photos (id, child_id, image_url)
Pickups (id, child_id, time, safe_word)
AuthorizedPersons (id, child_id, name, safe_word)
-Relationships
One parent → many children
One child → many activities
Each pickup → linked to a child
-Constraints
Email must be unique
Safe word required for pickup
Foreign keys must be valid
c. Technologies Used
List technologies, and languages used, including reasons for selection.
Backend: Python (Django) → easy, scalable, secure
Frontend: HTML, CSS, JavaScript → responsive UI
Database: MySQL / PostgreSQL → reliable data storage
d. User Interface Design
-Main Pages
Login/Register Page
Parent Dashboard (activities, photos, notifications)
Staff Dashboard (update activities)
Admin Panel (manage users)
-Design Features
Simple and clean layout
Easy navigation
Buttons for quick actions
Mobile-friendly design
e. Security Measures
- User authentication (login system)
- Password encryption (hashed passwords)
- Role-based access control (admin, staff, parent)
- Safe-word verification for pickups
- Secure data transmission (HTTPS)
- Data privacy protection
